  "remaining_required_native_adoption": [
    "UtilityRuntimeOwner still constructs legacy klog/error-handler/crash state and Go allocation/Unicode profiles. Map remaining HTTP/gateway/crash consumers, then remove unused machinery and registrations; no facade completion credit.",
    "HTTP-boundary LogEntry adapters still accept legacy SourceUrl/Headers producers. Adopt native protocol types and preserve Agones request fields and credential redaction.",
    "Queue storage/value/rate-limiter implementation still contains Go any/nil/hash/slice/numeric machinery. Replace it with native domain-key queues and selected Rust facilities while preserving deduplication, dirty/in-flight state, retry, delay and shutdown.",
    "Error-origin/source-format compatibility declarations and modules remain compiled for other legacy consumers. Native Agones errors no longer instantiate old fmt objects; map remaining callers before retirement.",
    "CRD readiness, discovery/serialization, admission, filesystem notifications, TLS reload, signal cleanup, feature/configuration consumers and whole-body/native-consumer reconciliation remain open in the canonical 13-gap M0003 list.",
    "Complete required scope across both routes and outputs before opening the global gate. All runtime/test/proof/compile assurance remains NOT_STARTED."
  ],
